@startuml transport_error_disconnection
title Disconnection via Transport Error — RMI vs. Socket

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA

note over GameNotifier, MatchManager
  This diagram covers the path where a disconnection is detected
  NOT by the health check thread, but during a normal outgoing callback
  (sendAsync): e.g. a RemoteException while pushing an update to the client.
end note

== RMI — Transport Error During sendAsync ==

participant "GameManager" as GM
participant "GameNotifier" as GN
participant "ClientHandlerRmi" as CHR
participant "ClientHandler\n(messageSender executor)" as ME
participant "VirtualViewRmi\n(stub)" as STUB
participant "ServerRmi\n(DisconnectionListener)" as DL
participant "MatchManager" as MM

GM -> GN : notifyMoveUpdate(tileDTO, currPlayer)
GN -> CHR : onMoveUpdate(tile, next)
note right of CHR
  delegates to:
  sendAsync(() -> clientStub.onMoveUpdate(tile, next))
end note
CHR -> ME : messageSender.submit(lambda)
ME -> STUB : clientStub.onMoveUpdate(tile, next)  [remote call]
STUB --> ME : RemoteException
ME -> CHR : handleTransportError(e)
note right of CHR
  if (tryMarkDisconnected()) {
    disconnectionListener.handleDisconnection(nickname)
  }
end note

CHR -> CHR : tryMarkDisconnected()


CHR -> DL : disconnectionListener.handleDisconnection(nickname)
DL -> MM : matchManager.disconnect(nickname)

== Socket — Transport Error During sendAsync ==

participant "GameManager" as GM2
participant "GameNotifier" as GN2
participant "ClientHandlerSocket" as CHS
participant "ClientHandler\n(messageSender executor)" as ME2
participant "ObjectOutputStream" as OOS
participant "MatchManager" as MM2

GM2 -> GN2 : notifyMoveUpdate(tileDTO, currPlayer)
GN2 -> CHS : onMoveUpdate(tile, next)
note right of CHS
  delegates to:
  sendAsync(() -> { out.writeObject(new MoveUpdateMessage(...)); out.reset(); out.flush(); })
end note
CHS -> ME2 : messageSender.submit(lambda)
ME2 -> OOS : out.writeObject(MoveUpdateMessage)
OOS --> ME2 : IOException
ME2 -> CHS : handleTransportError(e)
note right of CHS
  handleTransportError() delegates to:
  handleDisconnection(this.nickname)
end note

CHS -> CHS : handleDisconnection(nickname)


CHS -> MM2 : matchManager.disconnect(nickname)

note over CHS, MM2
  The read loop (run()) also catches IOException | ClassNotFoundException
  and calls handleDisconnection(nickname) directly —
  tryMarkDisconnected() ensures idempotency in both paths.
end note

@enduml